From 1760a09e6747392029c2144df4c456f80df19aa8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soulexit <metehan.tanriverdi01@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:41:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 80/84] panvk/jm: fix stale scalars in the bounded load
 vectorizer

panvk_vectorize_bounded_loads() collected a block's bounded loads, then
merged group after group, replacing the merged loads' defs. A later
group's stored address scalars (x, base, bound) can name one of those
defs (an index loaded from the same buffer), and its new address math
then used a freed def: NIR validation fails after the pass, and the
Bifrost compiler later frees corrupted ralloc memory (SIGSEGV in
unsafe_free from bi_compile_variant). The block is now rescanned after
each merged group.

Megabonk's DXVK compute shader 0x42fbee97 crashed vkCreateComputePipelines
on the Mali-G76 (soulexit/panvk-kirin990#10); it compiles now, also with
ASan and NIR validation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
index bcd538b9f00..560a83f4d76 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
@@ -668,6 +668,17 @@ panvk_vectorize_bounded_loads(nir_shader *nir)
       bool impl_progress = false;
 
       nir_foreach_block(block, impl) {
+         /* One group per scan: merging replaces the members' defs, and a
+          * later candidate's address (x, base, bound) may be one of them (an
+          * index loaded from the same buffer). Its stored scalar then named
+          * a freed def, and the new address math used it: NIR validation
+          * failed and the compiler later freed corrupted memory (Megabonk's
+          * compute shaders on the G76, issue #10). Rescanning after each
+          * group keeps every scalar live; merged loads are no longer
+          * bounded loads, so this ends. */
+         bool rescan = true;
+         while (rescan) {
+         rescan = false;
          /* The rewrites below free instructions: drop cached analysis. */
          _mesa_hash_table_clear(lsb_ht, NULL);
          util_dynarray_clear(&cands);
@@ -735,6 +746,9 @@ panvk_vectorize_bounded_loads(nir_shader *nir)
             stats[4]++;
             stats[5] += members;
             impl_progress = true;
+            rescan = true;
+            break;
+         }
          }
       }
 
